00:10:37,262 --> 00:10:39,306
but man, this would be
a nice place to live!"

265
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:41,600
Yeah, but so is this.

266
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:45,103
Yeah, I mean, if you move there,
you have to leave here.

267
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:47,481
I mean, how can you leave
this place?

268
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,986
Come on, Daddy,
listen to me!

269
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,530
It's like all of my life,
everyone has always told me,

270
00:10:55,572 --> 00:10:56,948
"You're a shoe!

271
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,659
You're a shoe,
you're a shoe,
you're a shoe!"

272
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,869
And then today,
I just stopped and I said,

273
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:03,746
"What if I don't want
to be a shoe?

274
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:05,499
What if I want to be
a-a purse?"

275
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,959
You know, or-or-or a hat?

276
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,171
No, I don't want you
to buy me a hat.

277
00:11:11,212 --> 00:11:14,048
I'm saying that I am a ha...
It's a metaphor, Daddy.

278
00:11:15,674 --> 00:11:17,718
You can see where
he'd have trouble.

279
00:11:20,305 --> 00:11:22,474
Well, maybe I'll just stay here
with Monica.

280
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:27,979
Well, I guess we've established
who's staying here with Monica.

281
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:31,774
Your money's mine, Green.

282
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:33,692
Your fly is open, Geller.

283
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:37,030
Oh, do you know
what I just realized?

284
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:40,492
"Joker" is "poker"
with a "J."

285
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:44,912
Coincidence?

286
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:47,374
Hey, that's
"Joe-incidence"
with a "c."

287
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:53,463
Ooh, look!

288
00:11:53,505 --> 00:11:55,465
Ugly Naked Guy lit
a bunch of candles.

289
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,553
ALL:
Ew!

290
00:11:59,594 --> 00:12:02,805
( all gasping )

291
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,932
That had to hurt.

292
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:06,560
Aw...
Aw...
Aw...

293
00:12:06,601 --> 00:12:09,062
Hey, it's your Thanksgiving,
too, you know?

294
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:11,690
Instead of watching football,
you could help.

295
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:14,568
GUYS:
We know.

296
00:12:14,609 --> 00:12:16,403
Rachel, you want to put
the marshmallows

297
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:18,112
in concentric circles.

298
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,074
No, Mon, you want to put them
in concentric circles.

299
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:23,784
I want to do this.

300
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:34,753
Every year.

301
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:37,591
( gasps )

302
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:39,217
JOEY:
It's stuck!

303
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:40,759
Well...

304
00:12:40,801 --> 00:12:42,095
step...

305
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:43,762
How did it get on?!

306
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:46,600
I put it on
to scare Chandler.

307
00:12:46,641 --> 00:12:47,934
Oh, my God!

308
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:50,520
Monica's going to
totally freak out!

309
00:12:50,562 --> 00:12:53,022
Plus, it smells
really bad in here.

310
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:54,773
Yeah, of course
it smells bad.

311
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:57,193
You have your head
inside a turkey's ass.

312
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,447
Oh, oh!
Monica.

313
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:01,656
Oh!

314
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:06,119
Hey, did you get the turkey...?
Oh, my God!

315
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,954
Oh, my God!

316
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:09,205
Who is that?

317
00:13:09,247 --> 00:13:12,292
It's Joey!

318
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,627
I got it.

319
00:13:13,668 --> 00:13:15,044
How 'bout, if we win,

320
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:17,505
they have to get
rid of the rooster?

321
00:13:17,547 --> 00:13:19,215
Ooh, that's interesting.

322
00:13:19,257 --> 00:13:22,510
If you win, we
give up the bird.

323
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:23,844
( shudders )

324
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,848
But if we win...

325
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,850
we get your apartment.

326
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:31,478
( Rachel scoffs )

327
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:33,187
JOEY:
Ooh-hoo-hoo
hoo-hoo!

328
00:13:33,229 --> 00:13:34,648
Deal!
Wha...?

329
00:13:34,689 --> 00:13:36,357
What?!

330
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:39,026
What was Monica's nickname when
she was a field hockey goalie?

331
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:39,778
Big Fat Goalie.

332
00:13:39,818 --> 00:13:40,403
Correct.

333
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:44,741
Rachel claims this
is her favorite movie.

334
00:13:44,783 --> 00:13:46,326
Dangerous Liaisons.

335
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:47,868
Correct.
Her actual favorite movie is?

336
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,162
Weekend at Bernie's.

337
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,997
Correct.

338
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:53,124
Monica categorizes her towels.

339
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,251
How many categories are there?

340
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:56,252
Okay, Everyday Use.

341
00:13:56,294 --> 00:13:57,337
Fancy.
Guest.

342
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:58,379
Fancy Guest.

343
00:13:58,421 --> 00:13:59,380
Two seconds.

344
00:13:59,422 --> 00:14:00,548
Ah... eleven?!

345
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:02,383
11, unbelievable.

346
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:03,884
11 is correct.

347
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:04,927
Yes!

348
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:06,638
( Joey cackles )

349
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,765
Chandler was how old when he
first touched a girl's breast?

350
00:14:08,807 --> 00:14:09,557
Fourteen?

351
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:10,266
No, 19.

352
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:12,059
Thanks, man.

353
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:13,978
Joey had
an imaginary childhood friend.

354
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,563
His name was?

355
00:14:15,605 --> 00:14:16,439
Maurice.
Correct.

356
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:17,565
His profession was...?

357
00:14:17,607 --> 00:14:18,899
Oh, space cowboy!
Correct.

358
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,570
What is Chandler Bing's job?

359
00:14:22,612 --> 00:14:23,780
Uh...

360
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:26,282
Oh...

361
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:28,075
Oh, gosh.

362
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:29,868
Ten seconds. You need this,
or you lose the game.

363
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:31,162
Oh!
It's, um...

364
00:14:31,204 --> 00:14:32,955
it has something
to do with transponding...

365
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:35,916
Oh, oh, oh, he's
a transpons...
transponster!

366
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:38,127
That's not even a word!

367
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:40,046
Oh!
No, I-I...

368
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:42,923
Oh, my...

369
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:44,217
Noooooo...!

370
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:48,596
( chuckles )

371
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:50,056
RACHEL:
You know what?

372
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:52,684
You are mean boys
who are just being mean.

373
00:14:52,726 --> 00:14:54,101
Hey, don't get mad at us.

374
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:56,187
No one forced you
to raise the stakes.

375
00:14:56,229 --> 00:14:57,355
That is not true.

376
00:14:57,397 --> 00:14:58,939
She did.
She forced me.

377
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,191
Hey, we'd still
be living here,

378
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:01,651
if you hadn't gotten
the question wrong.

379
00:15:01,693 --> 00:15:04,153
Well, it was a stupid,
unfair question.

380
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:05,988
Don't blame the questions.

381
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:09,325
Would you all stop yelling
in our apartment?

382
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,952
You are ruining
moving day for us.

383
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,496
Chandler!

384
00:15:15,498 --> 00:15:16,999
Chandler!

385
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:19,460
I saw what you were doing
through the window!

386
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:21,629
I saw what you were doing
to my sister.

387
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:22,756
Now, get out here!

388
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,216
Listen, we had a good run.

389
00:15:25,258 --> 00:15:27,301
You know, what was it?
Four-five months?

390
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:30,263
I mean, that's more than most
people have in a lifetime,

391
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:32,139
so good-bye, take care,
bye-bye, then.

392
00:15:34,225 --> 00:15:36,269
Hey, Ross.
What's up, bro?

393
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:39,689
What...

394
00:15:39,731 --> 00:15:42,483
the hell are you doing?!

395
00:15:42,525 --> 00:15:43,693
Hey, wh-what's going on?

396
00:15:43,735 --> 00:15:45,570
Well, I think-- I think--

397
00:15:45,612 --> 00:15:47,947
Ross knows about
me and Monica.

398
00:15:47,988 --> 00:15:51,826
( half-whispers ):
Dude, he's right there...

399
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:55,121
I thought you were
my best friend.

400
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:56,748
This is my sister.

401
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:59,834
My best friend and my sister--
I-I cannot believe this.

402
00:15:59,876 --> 00:16:02,670
Look, we're not
just messing around.

403
00:16:02,712 --> 00:16:04,004
I love her, okay?

404
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:05,799
I'm in love with her.

405
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:10,094
I am so sorry that you had
to find out this way.

406
00:16:10,136 --> 00:16:12,513
I'm sorry, but it's true.

407
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:14,265
I-I love him, too.

408
00:16:20,271 --> 00:16:23,065
My best friend and my sister!

409
00:16:25,735 --> 00:16:28,279
I cannot believe this!

410
00:16:29,656 --> 00:16:31,532
Well, this is the last
box of your clothes.

411
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:32,617
I'm just gonna label it

412
00:16:32,659 --> 00:16:34,661
"What were you thinking?"

413
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:38,372
Funny, 'cause I was just gonna
go across the hall

414
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:39,749
and write that on Chandler.

415
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:44,879
Okay, you guys, I don't mean
to make things worse,

416
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:47,674
but, um... I don't want to live
with Rachel anymore.

417
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:49,133
What?!
What?!

418
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:50,635
You're just
so mean to
each other.

419
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:52,428
And I don't want to end up
like that with Rachel.

420
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:53,972
I still like you.

421
00:16:54,012 --> 00:16:56,724
Well, Phoebe, that's fine,
because I'm not moving.

422
00:16:56,766 --> 00:16:58,434
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa.

423
00:16:58,476 --> 00:17:00,019
Phoebe, you gotta take her.

424
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,772
You know, I know I said
some really bad stuff about her,

425
00:17:02,814 --> 00:17:04,858
but you know, Rachel does have
some good qualities

426
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:06,108
that make her a good roommate.

427
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,319
She gets tons of catalogs.

428
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:09,737
And she'll fold down the pages

429
00:17:09,779 --> 00:17:11,447
of the things
that she thinks that I'd like.

430
00:17:11,489 --> 00:17:12,907
What else?

431
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:14,617
Well...

432
00:17:14,659 --> 00:17:16,118
When I take a shower,

433
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,955
she leaves me little notes
on the mirror.

434
00:17:18,997 --> 00:17:20,039
Yeah, I do.

435
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,332
I do do that.

436
00:17:21,374 --> 00:17:23,083
That's nice.

437
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:25,586
I like having things to read
in the bathroom.

438
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,965
When I fall asleep
on the couch

439
00:17:29,007 --> 00:17:30,299
after reading,

440
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:33,469
she covers me over
with a blanket.

441
00:17:33,511 --> 00:17:37,640
Well, you know,
I don't want you to be cold.

442
00:17:37,682 --> 00:17:40,393
And...

443
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:44,397
when I told her that I was going
to be moving in with Chandler,

444
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:46,816
she was really supportive.

445
00:17:48,526 --> 00:17:51,237
( voice breaking ):
You were so great.

446
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:55,324
You made it so easy.

447
00:17:56,659 --> 00:17:59,037
( sobbing ):
And now you
have to leave...

448
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:01,998
and I have to
live with a boy!

449
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,207
Oh...

450
00:18:03,249 --> 00:18:04,375
honey!

451
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:17,346
Hey.

452
00:18:18,389 --> 00:18:19,891
She really left.

453
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:22,184
Yeah, I know.

454
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:24,812
Thank you.

455
00:18:24,854 --> 00:18:26,647
No problem, roomie.

456
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:30,985
Thanks.

457
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:36,407
Can I ask you a question?

458
00:18:36,449 --> 00:18:37,658
Sure.

459
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:40,369
What the hell is
that dog doing here?

460
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:43,205
Little toast here.
Ding-ding...

461
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:45,917
I know this isn't exactly
the kind of Thanksgiving

462
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:47,460
that all of you planned,

463
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:51,129
but for me, this has been
really great, you know?

464
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:54,383
I think because
it didn't involve divorce

465
00:18:54,425 --> 00:18:56,260
or projectile vomiting.

466
00:18:59,013 --> 00:19:01,557
Anyway, I was just thinking,
I mean, if you'd gone to Vail,

467
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:03,392
or if you guys had been
with your family,

468
00:19:03,434 --> 00:19:05,103
or if you didn't have...

469
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:07,063
syphilis and stuff...

470
00:19:09,607 --> 00:19:12,318
...we wouldn't be all together,
you know?

471
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:14,821
So, I guess what I'm trying
to say is

472
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:16,363
that I'm very thankful

473
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:18,992
that all of
your Thanksgivings sucked.

474
00:19:19,993 --> 00:19:21,786
That's so sweet.

475
00:19:21,828 --> 00:19:23,788
Thank you...

476
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:25,164
Mmm!

477
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:28,042
And, hey, here's to
a lousy Christmas.

478
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:29,460
And a crappy New Year.

479
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:30,711
Hear, hear!

480
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:38,886
You can't move.

481
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:40,262
You just... you just can't.

482
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:41,388
Rachel's right.

483
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,099
This is where you guys belong.

484
00:19:43,141 --> 00:19:45,101
Yeah, you don't want
to live in Westchester.

485
00:19:45,143 --> 00:19:46,811
That's like the worst
of the Chesters.

486
00:19:46,853 --> 00:19:49,063
ROSS:
You know,
sometimes,

487
00:19:49,105 --> 00:19:52,441
when I'm alone in my apartment,
I look over here,

488
00:19:52,483 --> 00:19:54,902
and you guys are
just having dinner

489
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:58,781
or watching TV
or something, but...

490
00:19:58,823 --> 00:20:00,574
it makes me feel better.

491
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:03,243
And now when I
look over, who
am I gonna see?

492
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:04,871
The Gottliebs?

493
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:06,372
The Yangs?

494
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,666
They don't make
me feel so good.

495
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:12,545
Yeah, so-so
don't move, okay?

496
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:13,713
Just stay here, and...

497
00:20:13,754 --> 00:20:15,464
maybe close
your blinds at night.

498
00:20:15,506 --> 00:20:16,590
Hey.

499
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:20,260
( phone rings )

500
00:20:20,302 --> 00:20:22,638
( sighs )

501
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,057
Hello?

502
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:29,645
It's Nancy.
They responded to our offer.

503
00:20:29,687 --> 00:20:31,105
And?

504
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:36,027
Okay, thanks.

505
00:20:37,862 --> 00:20:39,238
They passed.

506
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:43,743
They said they wouldn't go
a penny under the asking price.

507
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:45,203
We can't afford that.

508
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,829
I know.

509
00:20:48,539 --> 00:20:50,457
Well, there you go.

510
00:20:55,046 --> 00:20:56,923
JOEY:
I'm really
sorry, you guys.

511
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,382
Yeah, I'm sorry, too.

512
00:20:58,424 --> 00:21:00,300
I'm even more sorry
that that phone call

513
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:01,761
didn't come
before I told you

514
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:03,345
about looking through
the window.

515
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:05,305
RACHEL:
Yeah, well,

516
00:21:05,347 --> 00:21:06,891
we're going
to let you be alone.

517
00:21:06,933 --> 00:21:07,934
You going to be okay?

518
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:08,976
Yeah, we'll be okay.

519
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:11,270
I love you guys.

520
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,898
Hey, you know,

521
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:15,858
I'm really sorry I wasn't
more supportive before.

522
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:18,318
Oh, it's okay.
We understand.

523
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,737
Yeah, and about this Nancy...

524
00:21:19,779 --> 00:21:21,906
if you're not sleeping
with her, should I?

525
00:21:29,205 --> 00:21:31,624
I know there'll be other houses,
but I just...

526
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:33,042
I love that one so much.

527
00:21:33,084 --> 00:21:34,752
Yeah.

528
00:21:34,794 --> 00:21:37,421
Well, it's a good thing
we got it, then.

529
00:21:38,631 --> 00:21:39,715
What?!

530
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:41,092
We got the house!

531
00:21:41,134 --> 00:21:43,052
Oh, my God!

532
00:21:43,094 --> 00:21:44,845
I just didn't want to tell you
in front of them.

533
00:21:44,887 --> 00:21:46,597
Oh, my God! We got it?
We got the house?!

534
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:47,723
We're getting the house!

535
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:49,058
Oh!

536
00:21:51,144 --> 00:21:52,228
Mmm!

537
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:54,021
We're getting a house.

538
00:21:54,063 --> 00:21:55,439
And a baby!

539
00:21:55,481 --> 00:21:57,024
We're growing up.

540
00:21:58,192 --> 00:21:59,902
We sure are.

541
00:21:59,944 --> 00:22:01,946
So, who's gonna tell them?

542
00:22:01,988 --> 00:22:03,781
Not it!
Not it.
Damn it!

543
00:22:09,162 --> 00:22:10,579
And Rachel,
this is yours.

544
00:22:10,621 --> 00:22:12,248
( screams ):
What are these for?!

545
00:22:12,290 --> 00:22:13,457
You'll see.
All right.

546
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:14,875
Everybody
open them.
Okay.

547
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:17,711
( gasps )

548
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:19,839
Oh, wow, this
is so beautiful!

549
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:23,383
Oh, these are the ones
I was looking at in the store.

550
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:24,384
I know.

551
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:25,343
I love this.

552
00:22:25,385 --> 00:22:27,888
A meatball sub!?

553
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:29,473
Thanks!

554
00:22:29,515 --> 00:22:31,184
Seriously, you guys.
What's going on?

555
00:22:31,225 --> 00:22:32,643
What are these for?

556
00:22:32,685 --> 00:22:35,188
Well, I didn't know
how to tell you before, but...

557
00:22:35,229 --> 00:22:36,189
we got the house.

558
00:22:36,230 --> 00:22:38,232
Enjoy!

559
00:22:38,274 --> 00:22:42,360
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

560
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:44,071
What did they say?

